    "content": "Patriots' Day (observed third Monday in April, April 20, 2026) is a civic holiday in Massachusetts and Maine commemorating the opening battles of the American Revolutionary War at Lexington and Concord in 1775. It features battle reenactments, the Boston Marathon, and is often marked by the 2016 film Patriots Day depicting the 2013 marathon bombing.Key Aspects of Patriots' Day:Historical Significance: Commemorates the \"shot heard 'round the world\" on April 19, 1775, marking the start of the Revolutionary War.Key Events (2026):Boston Marathon: Traditionally held on this Monday, running from Hopkinton to Boston.Battle Reenactments: Held in Lexington (Battle Green) and Concord (North Bridge).Monday Holiday: State and municipal offices, schools, and some businesses in Massachusetts are closed.Events: Parade in Lexington, ceremonies at Minute Man National Historical Park, and a Boston Red Sox home game.Patriots Day (2016 Film) Analysis:Plot: The film directed by Peter Berg centers on the 2013 Boston Marathon bombing and the intense, days-long manhunt for the terrorists.Characters/Cast: Features a mix of fictionalized and real-life characters, including Mark Wahlberg (Sgt. Tommy Saunders), Kevin Bacon (FBI Agent Richard DesLauriers), John Goodman (Comm. Ed Davis), J.K. Simmons (Sgt. Jeffrey Pugliese), and Michelle Monaghan (Carol Saunders).Producers: The film was produced by Scott Stuber, Mark Wahlberg, Hutch Parker, Dylan Clark, Stephen Levinson, Peter Berg, and Michael Radutzky.Tone: A fast-paced, gritty police procedural that emphasizes \"Boston Strong\" resilience, receiving positive notes for its intense reenactment of the investigation.Watch the official trailer for the 2016 film 'Patriots Day':44sPATRIOTS DAY - OFFICIAL MOVIE TRAILER - HDCBS FilmsYouTube• Nov 14, 2016Patriots' Day 2026 Schedule:Events: Spanning from April 17 to April 21, 2026, featuring dawn salutes, reenactments, and parades.Operational Changes: While state services close, federal services like the U.S. Postal Service remain open.",
